**Repository observation shaping the design:** with no schema, split or parameter definitions locally, everything dataset-dependent is quarantined as numbered assumptions [A-1..A-7] with its required confirmation, while everything under our control is pinned explicitly (seed manifest, hashed split file, nested-superset assertions, fixed search spaces, 10-trial budget, thresholds, prediction-array outputs for reanalysis).", "assumptions": ["[A-1] DrivAerNet++ parametric pool ~10,000 samples; we build our own 80/10/10 body-variant-stratified split (~8k/1k/1k); no canonical public parametric split is honored. Needs confirmation: actual sample count, which fixes N_max and the ladder top.", "[A-2] Target is total drag coefficient Cd; CdA is only a fixed-reference-area rescaling, and front/rear CdA decomposition is unavailable.", "[A-3] The 26 inputs are purely geometric, excluding driving conditions; primary analysis uses the nominal/0-degree-yaw subset so x->Cd is a function. Needs confirmation: parameter names/bounds and nominal-yaw sample count.", "[A-4] Cd spans ~0.23-0.50 and is near-homoscedastic, so no target transform in the primary arm (log-Cd is a sensitivity arm).", "[A-5] Body variant is an explicit parameter, enabling stratification and the hold-a-body-type-out regime; the held-out variant is fixed in the manifest before any run.", "[A-6] Continuous Cd regression is the endpoint; within-5/10-count rates are derived decision views, not a class-of-excellence endpoint.", "Standardization is fit once on the full TRAIN pool and frozen across all N; per-subset refit exists only as a sensitivity arm.", "Equalized tuning: 10 validation-driven trials per (architecture, N, seed) for every tunable arm plus one refit at the VAL-best config; A1 and A0 exempt, exemption documented in advance.", "Exact GP capped at N <= 1,600 (Nystrom m=500 above); KRR runs to N_max; binding compute constraints are the exact kernel solves and the high-capacity tabular net under CPU-only conditions.", "Any future run requires numpy, scipy, scikit-learn, pandas/h5py, CPU PyTorch and one GBT library plus the DrivAerNet++ parametric table to be provisioned - a prerequisite, not a finding; none exist in the inspected workspace and the network is disabled.", "Wall-clock figures (~23 h single-threaded-equivalent for deep arms, ~1-2 h wall clock at 48-56 workers x 4 threads, ~half a day for the suite) are planning estimates, not measurements.", "CFD repeatability / irreducible noise floor assumed small (~1-2 Cd counts); the design includes a noise-floor probe precisely because this is unknown."], "uncertainties": ["If the usable pool is much smaller than assumed (e.g. ~5k total / ~4k train), the 8-point ladder compresses, the exponent is weakly identified, and claim (b) may have to fall back to monotone-trend plus paired-difference evidence.", "If models reach the CFD noise floor by N ~1,600, curves saturate, L_inf and b become collinear, and architecture gaps may sit inside test-set sampling error; mitigations are the saturation label and paired bootstrap CIs, not a fix.", "Under CPU-only conditions the deep arms (A6/A7) may be under-trained at the equalized 10-trial budget, biasing the deep-vs-tree crossover against them; the crossover-N claim carries an explicit compute caveat.", "Whether DrivAerNet++ ships a recommended parametric split that reviewers expect us to use; if so our self-built split must be justified or aligned.", "Whether enough nominal-yaw samples exist per body variant to support both stratified nesting and the hold-a-body-type-out regime; if not the secondary arm shrinks to 2 sizes x 2 seeds or drops.", "Test-set sampling error from a single frozen 10% TEST: absolute levels could shift under a different partition; paired bootstrap handles comparisons but not this.", "The mixed-effects interaction test assumes roughly homogeneous residual variance across architectures; if residual diagnostics (checked before inspecting curves) reject this, the pre-registered log-RMSE or rank-based variant becomes primary."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8468940ef90cdbb8", "tool_call": {"id": "chatcmpl-tool-8468940ef90cdbb8", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{"stage": "result", "answer": "# FINAL EXPERIMENT DESIGN (design-only; nothing has been run \u2014 no results are reported or implied)\n\n**Question.** Does surrogate predictive performance for aerodynamic drag improve with training-set size, and does that scaling behaviour differ across model architectures? Two-factor learning-curve design: **architecture \u00d7 training-set size**, parametric-only inputs, one frozen TEST set.\n\n**Global conventions.** Dataset-dependent numbers are written as `[A-n]` assumptions with the confirmation each still needs. Wall-clock numbers are order-of-magnitude design estimates, not measurements. Items marked **[V]** were verified by inspecting this machine.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Data model, split, and nesting protocol\n\n**Unit of analysis.** One sample = 26 geometric parameters `x \u2208 R\u00b2\u2076` \u2192 scalar total drag coefficient `Cd` from the CFD solve. Parametric-only: no mesh, point cloud, pressure or wall-shear fields.\n\n**Pool and split.** The DrivAerNet++ parametric table (parameters + force-derived coefficients) is the only ingested artifact. No canonical public *parametric* split is relied upon; we build and freeze our own:\n- `TRAIN`/`VAL`/`TEST` = 80/10/10 % stratified on body variant (notchback/estateback/fastback) \u2192 `[A-1]` pool \u2248 10,000 \u2192 \u2248 8,000/1,000/1,000. *Needs confirmation: actual sample count and the column encoding body variant.*\n- Split generated once from seed 20261023, written to `split_v1.csv` (sample id \u2192 partition, stratum), hash-logged, reused by every run; TEST never regenerated.\n- `[A-2]` Target = total `Cd`. *Needs confirmation: exact target column, and whether CdA is a fixed-area rescaling (then reported as such).*\n- `[A-3]` Driving conditions (yaw, road level) are separate from the 26 geometric parameters. Primary arm restricts the pool to nominal (0\u00b0 yaw) samples so `x \u2192 Cd` is a well-defined function, with the 26 geometric parameters as the only features. *Needs confirmation: parameter names/bounds and number of nominal-yaw samples. If yaw-swept samples dominate, yaw becomes an extra input \u2014 declared a design change, not absorbed silently.*\n\n**Nested subsets (core integrity device).** For each seed `s \u2208 {0..4}`: partition `TRAIN` by body variant, permute each stratum with `RandomState(1000+s)`, and take subset `N_k` = first `round(N_k \u00b7 stratum_share)` of each stratum. Hence `S_1 \u2282 \u2026 \u2282 S_K` as **strict supersets** with body-variant composition constant to <1 sample across N. Runtime assertions: `S_k \u2286 S_{k+1}`, stratum-share tolerance, `S_K \u2229 TEST = \u2205`.\n\n**Size ladder** (8 log-spaced points): `N \u2208 {50, 100, 200, 400, 800, 1600, 3200, N_max}`, `N_max = |TRAIN|` \u2248 6,400\u20138,000 `[A-1]`; ~2\u00d7 spacing is what makes an exponent estimable.\n\n**Preprocessing.** Inputs standardized with statistics fit **once on the full TRAIN pool**, frozen across all N and architectures, reused on VAL/TEST. Target: raw `Cd`. Sensitivity arms only: log-Cd target; per-subset scaler refit.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architectures (factor explicitly scoped)\n\nBecause inputs are 26-dim vectors, **\"differ across model architectures\" is scoped to the tabular family**; CNN/GNO/point-net/field surrogates are out of scope by construction.\n\n| ID | Architecture | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| A0 | Constant (train-mean Cd) | no-signal **floor**, no fit |\n| A1 | Ridge / elastic-net linear | linearity floor |\n| A2 | Kernel ridge RBF; exact GP (ARD-Matern-5/2) capped at N \u2264 1,600, Nystr\u00f6m m=500 above | strong small-N + uncertainty |\n| A3 | Random forest (600 trees) | bagging family |\n| A4 | Gradient-boosted trees (HistGB/LightGBM/XGBoost) | cheapest tabular front-runner; secondary-arm member |\n| A5 | MLP-mid 2\u00d7128, early stopping | standard deep tabular |\n| A6 | MLP-deep 4\u00d7256 residual + LayerNorm | capacity/depth probe |\n| A7 | FT-Transformer (d=64, 3 layers, 4 heads) | one high-capacity tabular net |\n| A-null | Shuffled-label control on A4 and A6 | pipeline-artifact control |\n\nSearch spaces fixed in a manifest before any run: A1 \u03b1 \u2208 log-U(1e-3,1e3); A2 \u03b3 \u2208 log-U(2\u207b\u2074,2\u00b2), \u03b1 \u2208 log-U(1e-3,1e2); A3 max-features \u2208 {0.3,0.5,0.7,1.0}, min-samples-leaf \u2208 {1,2,4,8}; A4 n-est \u2264 2,000 w/ early stopping, lr \u2208 log-U(0.01,0.3), depth \u2208 {3,5,7}; A5/A6 width/depth/lr/dropout/weight-decay; A7 d/heads/lr/dropout. Early stopping (A5\u2013A7) uses **only** the frozen VAL.\n\n**Fairness rule.** Exactly **10 validation-driven trials per (architecture, N, seed)** for every tunable arm \u2014 budget independent of N and architecture \u2014 then one refit on `S_N` with the VAL-best config and the same seed. A1 (\u22642 trials) and A0 (0) are exempt; exemption documented in advance.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Metrics\n\n- **Primary:** test **RMSE** on Cd. **Co-primary reporting:** MAE, R\u00b2, Cd-count error (1 count = 0.001 Cd).\n- **Derived decision views:** fraction within \u22645 and \u226410 counts; NRMSE/MAPE (secondary; `[A-4]` Cd \u2248 0.23\u20130.50, so MAPE \u2248 proportional to MAE).\n- **Uncertainty calibration (A2, descriptive):** NLL, PICP@90.\n- No class-of-excellence label as a first-class endpoint.\n- **Noise-floor probe:** duplicate/near-duplicate parameter vectors give a direct CFD-repeatability estimate if present; otherwise A2 predictive variance and A4/A6 residuals at N_max bound the floor. Reported beside every curve so saturation is read against a floor, not against zero.\n- All metrics recomputed from saved per-cell predictions (`preds/{arch}_{N}_{seed}_{regime}.npz`) so no refit is needed for reanalysis.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Runs, cost, feasibility\n\n| Arm | Top-level fits | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Primary 7 trainable \u00d7 8 sizes \u00d7 5 seeds | **280** | + ~2,400 inner tuning fits (10 trials \u00d7 240 tunable cells) |\n| A0 floor 8 \u00d7 5 | 40 | no fit |\n| A-null 2 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 3 | 24 | sizes {100,400,1600,N_max} |\n| log-Cd sensitivity 2 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 3 | 24 | |\n| Scaler-refit sensitivity 2 \u00d7 4 \u00d7 3 | 24 | |\n| **Secondary regime arm** (A4, A5) \u00d7 4 sizes \u00d7 3 seeds \u00d7 2 regimes | 48 | new pool for extrapolation \u2192 all cells new |\n| **Total** | **\u2248 440 + \u2248 2,400 tuning** | |\n\nWall-clock reasoning (estimates): ridge/RF/HGB seconds; KRR at N_max is O(N\u00b3) (6,400\u00b3 \u2248 2.6e11 flops) \u2192 tens of seconds, acceptable; exact GP capped at N \u2264 1,600 with Nystr\u00f6m above (the reason for the cap). CPU MLPs on 8k\u00d726: ~30\u201360 s per trial fit \u2192 A5+A6 \u2248 10 h sequential; A7 \u2248 13 h sequential. Deep arms dominate: ~23 h single-threaded-equivalent \u2192 **~1\u20132 h wall clock** at ~48\u201356 workers \u00d7 4 threads on 224 cores; whole suite \u2248 **half a day wall clock, a few dozen core-hours**; RAM never binding (largest dense array ~330 MB).\n\n**Environment as verified [V]:** `/workspace` holds only `task.json`; no DrivAerNet++ data, metadata, split files, scripts or model code anywhere on the filesystem; Python 3.14.4 with **no** numpy/scipy/pandas/sklearn/torch/xgboost/lightgbm/h5py; pip unusable offline and DNS resolution fails (network disabled); no GPU; 224 CPUs; ~1,931 GB free RAM; `/workspace` writable.\n\n**Requirement on any future run (prerequisite, not finding):** provision `numpy`, `scipy`, `scikit-learn`, `pandas`/`h5py`, CPU `torch`, one GBT library, plus the parametric table; plus a committed seed manifest and versioned config manifest so \"pre-registered\" is checkable. None exists here, so no part of this design has been or can be executed as-is.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Analysis plan and pre-registered decision rules\n\nUnit of analysis: per-(arch, N, seed) test metric \u2192 280 cells \u00d7 5 seeds = 1,400 primary observations. CIs: paired test-set bootstrap (10,000 resamples, identical indices across arms and N so comparisons stay paired) as primary; seed-level bootstrap as secondary.\n\n**(a) \"Improves with training-set size\" \u2014 per architecture.** *Supported* iff all three, Holm\u2013Bonferroni across the 7 trainable arms:\n1. Spearman \u03c1(test RMSE, log\u2081\u2080N) averaged over seeds \u2264 **\u22120.90**, bootstrap 95% CI upper bound < 0;\n2. RMSE reduction from `N_min=50` to `N_max` \u2265 **5 %** *or* \u2265 **1 Cd count** absolute, whichever is larger, paired CI excluding 0;\n3. At `N_max`, RMSE beats A0 (train-mean), paired seed-level bootstrap p < 0.05.\n\n**Saturation label (pre-registered so a flat curve isn't mislabeled \"size-insensitive\"):** if (1) fails but RMSE(N_max) is within **2 %** of RMSE(N=1,600), report *saturated / exponent unidentifiable over the observed ladder*.\n\n**(b) \"Differs across architectures.\"** *Supported* iff all three:\n1. Interaction `RMSE ~ log10(N) * architecture + (1|seed)` (mixed model; log-RMSE robustness variant) significant, Wald/LRT p < 0.05, Holm-corrected;\n2. Some architecture pair has power-law exponents `b` differing with bootstrap CI excluding 0, from `L(N) = L\u221e + a\u00b7N^(\u2212b)` fit per arm by nonlinear least squares on seed-averaged curves (`L\u221e` reported and flagged weakly identified when its CI spans 0 or `L\u221e < 0`);\n3. Practical significance: seed-averaged RMSE gap \u2265 **1 Cd count** at \u2265 2 ladder points, paired CI excluding 0.\n\n**Rank stability and crossovers.** Kendall's W within each N with bootstrap CI; best arm per N; crossover `N*` for A4 vs A5/A6 by interpolation with bootstrap CI, reported only if the CI lies inside [50, N_max], otherwise \"no crossover within the observed range\". Descriptive: error-vs-N bands, per-body-variant error decomposition, A2 uncertainty vs N.\n\n**Control expectations fixed in advance.** A-null must be flat in N and \u2248 A0 level \u2014 if A-null *improves* with N, subset generation or evaluation is broken and no claim is made. A0 is the no-signal floor all curves are plotted against. log-Cd and per-subset scaler refit must not alter any (a)/(b) conclusion; if they do, the conclusion is reported as preprocessing-dependent.\n\n**Secondary regime arm (outside the primary grid).** R1 interpolation = the primary split; R2 hold-a-body-type-out = one body variant removed from TRAIN/VAL and used as TEST `[A-5]` (variant fixed in the manifest pre-run; all-three-fold variant preferred if budget allows). Arms A4 and A5 only, sizes {100, 400, 1600, N_max(R2)} (ladder truncated because removing a body variant shrinks the pool), 3 seeds; TEST definition frozen per regime. Pre-registered expectation to test rather than assume: the A4\u2013A5 gap widens in R2 relative to R1. Descriptive only \u2014 it can neither rescue nor weaken the primary claims.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Assumptions needing confirmation\n\n`[A-1]` pool \u2248 10,000 \u2192 8k/1k/1k and `N_max`; `[A-2]` target column = total Cd (CdA only as fixed-area rescaling); `[A-3]` 26 inputs are geometric only, nominal-yaw subset adequate; `[A-4]` Cd range \u2248 0.23\u20130.50 (justifies raw scale); `[A-5]` body variant available as an explicit parameter; `[A-6]` no released canonical parametric split must be honored; `[A-7]` CFD noise floor \u2264 ~2 counts. All derive from external recall, not from this repository, which contains none of them.\n\n## 7. Limitations\n\n1. **Unverifiable data specifics here.** If the pool is much smaller (e.g. ~5k total / ~4k train), the ladder compresses and exponent estimation weakens; if `N_max < 2,000`, replace power-law claims with monotone-trend + paired-difference claims only.\n2. **Early saturation / noise floor.** If models reach CFD repeatability by N \u2248 1,600, the informative region is short, `L\u221e` and `b` become collinear, and rankings can be decided inside noise. Mitigations: noise-floor probe, saturation label, paired CIs \u2014 not a fix.\n3. **Exponents from 8 log-spaced points** are fragile; `b` is never reported alone, always with CI and alongside the model-free trend/paired-difference evidence.\n4. **CPU-only bias against deep arms.** A6/A7 may be under-trained at the equalized 10-trial budget relative to a GPU sweep, biasing the deep-vs-tree crossover; stated whenever `N*` is reported.\n5. **Equalized tuning is a fairness convention, not an optimum;** a per-N adaptive budget could reorder arms.\n6. **Single frozen 10 % TEST** means partition composition enters absolute levels; paired resampling handles comparisons but not this.\n7. **Design-only status.** No model was fitted, no curve exists; every quantity above is a design parameter, estimate, or assumption awaiting confirmation.", "evidence": "**Verified on this machine ([V], basis of the feasibility section):** `ls -la /workspace` \u2192 only `task.json` (752 B), writable; `find / -maxdepth 3 -iname \"*drivaer*\"` \u2192 no matches; `/data`, `/datasets`, `/mnt`, `/opt` absent; no CSV/HDF5/parquet, no split file, no scripts, no requirements/environment file. `importlib.util.find_spec` \u2192 False for numpy, scipy, pandas, sklearn, torch, xgboost, lightgbm, catboost, matplotlib, h5py, open3d, GPy, keras, tensorflow, joblib, sympy, plotly; `/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages` (250 entries) is Debian system tooling only. Install path closed: pip 25.1.1 present but `pip download numpy` \u2192 ImportError traceback, no local wheels, no cache, and `urlopen('https://pypi.org')` \u2192 `URLError: [Errno -3] Temporary failure in name resolution`. Hardware: Python 3.14.4, `nproc` 224, `free -g` 2011 total / 1931 available, no swap, gpu_enabled=false per the environment block.\n\n**Arithmetic/complexity checks (stdlib python run here):** 7 trainable archs \u00d7 8 sizes \u00d7 5 seeds = 280 primary fits; +40 A0 evaluations; +24 A-null; +24 log-Cd; +24 scaler; +48 regime-arm fits = 440 top-level; 10 trials \u00d7 240 tunable cells = 2,400 inner tuning fits. 6,400\u00b3 = 2.62e11 \u2192 motivates the exact-GP cap at N \u2264 1,600 and marks KRR-at-N_max as tens of seconds. Deep-arm sizing: 45 s \u00d7 10 trials \u00d7 80 cells \u2248 10.0 h; 120 s \u00d7 10 \u00d7 40 \u2248 13.3 h; \u2248 23 h sequential \u2192 ~1 h at 56 workers (224 cores / 4 threads) \u2014 the basis for the wall-clock statement.\n\n**Repository observation shaping the design:** with no schema, split or parameter definitions locally, everything dataset-dependent is quarantined as numbered assumptions [A-1..A-7] with its required confirmation, while everything under our control is pinned explicitly (seed manifest, hashed split file, nested-superset assertions, fixed search spaces, 10-trial budget, thresholds, prediction-array outputs for reanalysis).", "assumptions": ["[A-1] DrivAerNet++ parametric pool ~10,000 samples; we build our own 80/10/10 body-variant-stratified split (~8k/1k/1k); no canonical public parametric split is honored. Needs confirmation: actual sample count, which fixes N_max and the ladder top.", "[A-2] Target is total drag coefficient Cd; CdA is only a fixed-reference-area rescaling, and front/rear CdA decomposition is unavailable.", "[A-3] The 26 inputs are purely geometric, excluding driving conditions; primary analysis uses the nominal/0-degree-yaw subset so x->Cd is a function. Needs confirmation: parameter names/bounds and nominal-yaw sample count.", "[A-4] Cd spans ~0.23-0.50 and is near-homoscedastic, so no target transform in the primary arm (log-Cd is a sensitivity arm).", "[A-5] Body variant is an explicit parameter, enabling stratification and the hold-a-body-type-out regime; the held-out variant is fixed in the manifest before any run.", "[A-6] Continuous Cd regression is the endpoint; within-5/10-count rates are derived decision views, not a class-of-excellence endpoint.", "Standardization is fit once on the full TRAIN pool and frozen across all N; per-subset refit exists only as a sensitivity arm.", "Equalized tuning: 10 validation-driven trials per (architecture, N, seed) for every tunable arm plus one refit at the VAL-best config; A1 and A0 exempt, exemption documented in advance.", "Exact GP capped at N <= 1,600 (Nystrom m=500 above); KRR runs to N_max; binding compute constraints are the exact kernel solves and the high-capacity tabular net under CPU-only conditions.", "Any future run requires numpy, scipy, scikit-learn, pandas/h5py, CPU PyTorch and one GBT library plus the DrivAerNet++ parametric table to be provisioned - a prerequisite, not a finding; none exist in the inspected workspace and the network is disabled.", "Wall-clock figures (~23 h single-threaded-equivalent for deep arms, ~1-2 h wall clock at 48-56 workers x 4 threads, ~half a day for the suite) are planning estimates, not measurements.", "CFD repeatability / irreducible noise floor assumed small (~1-2 Cd counts); the design includes a noise-floor probe precisely because this is unknown."], "uncertainties": ["If the usable pool is much smaller than assumed (e.g. ~5k total / ~4k train), the 8-point ladder compresses, the exponent is weakly identified, and claim (b) may have to fall back to monotone-trend plus paired-difference evidence.", "If models reach the CFD noise floor by N ~1,600, curves saturate, L_inf and b become collinear, and architecture gaps may sit inside test-set sampling error; mitigations are the saturation label and paired bootstrap CIs, not a fix.", "Under CPU-only conditions the deep arms (A6/A7) may be under-trained at the equalized 10-trial budget, biasing the deep-vs-tree crossover against them; the crossover-N claim carries an explicit compute caveat.", "Whether DrivAerNet++ ships a recommended parametric split that reviewers expect us to use; if so our self-built split must be justified or aligned.", "Whether enough nominal-yaw samples exist per body variant to support both stratified nesting and the hold-a-body-type-out regime; if not the secondary arm shrinks to 2 sizes x 2 seeds or drops.", "Test-set sampling error from a single frozen 10% TEST: absolute levels could shift under a different partition; paired bootstrap handles comparisons but not this.", "The mixed-effects interaction test assumes roughly homogeneous residual variance across architectures; if residual diagnostics (checked before inspecting curves) reject this, the pre-registered log-RMSE or rank-based variant becomes primary."], "summary": "Final design: architecture x training-size learning curves on DrivAerNet++"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b17c60f9-ee38-4c38-b033-2d749a77bb9d", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Final design: architecture x training-size learning curves on DrivAerNet++", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
